{% doc %}
  Prints "true" while the 10% welcome offer is paused for a store-wide sale,
  "false" otherwise. The welcome popup, its reopen tab and the product-page
  "sign up for 10% off" line all check it, so a shopper is never shown the 10%
  offer next to a bigger sale.

  Current pause: the LMNY20 Black Friday sale (20% off all jewelry). It ends at
  11:59:59 PM New York time on 1 December 2026, the code's end date in Shopify
  Admin -> Discounts (1796187599 = 2026-12-02T04:59:59Z). The offer returns by
  itself after that. To pause again for a later sale, set paused_until to that
  sale's end as a Unix timestamp; leave it in the past to keep the offer on.

  @example
  {%- capture welcome_paused -%}{% render 'welcome-offer-paused' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign paused_until = 1796187599
  assign now_ts = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  if now_ts < paused_until
    echo 'true'
  else
    echo 'false'
  endif
-%}
